WEBVTT

00:40:28.958 --> 00:40:30.976
EP: Because the way it gets rationalized

00:40:31.000 --> 00:40:33.559
is people say, "It's just
not important enough for me.

00:40:33.583 --> 00:40:36.684
It's not worth the conversation.
It's not worth getting into it."

00:40:36.708 --> 00:40:38.434
And it's all these rationalizations

00:40:38.458 --> 00:40:40.934
that kind of say,
"It doesn't really matter."

00:40:40.958 --> 00:40:43.934
But meanwhile, at every step of the game,

00:40:43.958 --> 00:40:47.559
you're foregoing you
because you literally experience

00:40:47.583 --> 00:40:53.393
that the relationship only continues
if the other people are pleased with you.

00:40:53.417 --> 00:40:55.643
AG: Which is a pretty sad
state of affairs,

00:40:55.667 --> 00:40:58.143
if that's what it takes
to maintain a relationship.

00:40:58.167 --> 00:41:01.893
EP: So how did you learn to tolerate
conflict, tension, disagreement?